  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically preferring the lottery that is more right-skewed (i.e., one where a larger portion of the probability is assigned to unfavorable outcomes compared to favorable ones). To assess skewness, we need to compare the probabilities of favorable versus unfavorable outcomes. In both lotteries, the favorable outcome is the positive monetary amount (4000 for A, 3000 for B), and the unfavorable outcome is 0 euros. Lottery A assigns 20% probability to the favorable outcome and 80% to the unfavorable; Lottery B assigns 25% to the favorable and 75% to the unfavorable. Thus, Lottery A has a higher probability mass on the unfavorable outcome (80% vs 75%), making it more right-skewed than B. Therefore, according to the decision reason, Lottery A should be preferred because it is more right-skewed.",
